# (servers other processes connect to are started with "wait", as a client's own StartServer does: two camenuserver instances
# racing over the same SQL database made its first start fail with "database table is locked")
# What pheshellsel starts before Orbit's launcher (the format of core's s4start.txt). "wait <exe>" = start and wait for its
# rendezvous; "waitdir" = wait until a folder exists; a plain exe = fire and forget. Bare names are found in \sys\bin of
# every drive, so the package may sit on any of them.
rightsserver.exe
waitdir c:\system\temp\ 3000
wait hbthemeserver.exe
wait hbdevicedialogappserver.exe
qsfwdatabasemanagerserver.exe
qpspathmapperserver.exe
wait scrserver.exe
wait camenuserver.exe
softwaretransactionservices.exe
stsserver.exe
